## FAQ

**How fresh is the data?**
Every store is read once a day; the run is due at 06:17 UTC (early morning US time){% if bfcm_runs == 4 %}, and four times a day (00:17, 06:17, 12:17 and 18:17 UTC) from 26 November to 1 December{% endif %}. Each row shows when its current price was first seen, and the [last run badge]({{ repo_url }}/actions/workflows/daily.yml) shows the time of the latest run. {{ sched.delivered }} of {{ sched.slots }} due runs so far were delivered. {% if sched.on_time_since %}Since the on-time trigger took over from GitHub's scheduler, {{ on_time.value }} started on time (within {{ sched.on_time_window_h }} hours).{% else %}From the next run on, each run is started on time by a direct trigger, with GitHub's schedule kept as the fallback.{% endif %} {{ sched.note }}

**What happens when a site changes?**
The checks notice it: a run that looks wrong is held and I get an alert, while the last good data stays live. I fix the collector, usually the same day, and the next run fills the gap.

**Which formats can I get?**
Your data, in the format your team already uses: CSV, Excel (XLSX), JSON, SQL file (PostgreSQL / MySQL), SQLite, Parquet, Google Sheets, email or webhook. Excel and CSV are the default; other formats cost nothing extra. This repository delivers CSV, Parquet{% if pub.sheet %}, a Google Sheet{% endif %} and a dashboard.

**How far back does the history go?**
The daily summary goes back to {{ since_text }} and is never pruned. The change logs in this repository keep the last 30 days, and every version of every price stays in the monthly history files in the releases.

**Can you track my competitors' sites?**
Yes, if the information is public, such as prices, sales and stock on product pages. I check each site first and tell you what can be collected and how often, before any work starts.

**Is it legal and polite?**
It reads only public pages, follows each site's published rules (robots.txt), goes slowly, stops when a site asks, and collects no personal data. Site owners can ask for removal at any time (see [Data use and compliance](#data-use-and-compliance)).

**How does pricing work?**
After the free sample, you get a quote: a fixed monthly price for a running monitor, or a one-time price for a single collection. No hourly billing.

